cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use hmd-statusline in your work, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "hmd-statusline: a terminal statusline for AI coding sessions"
abstract: >-
  hmd-statusline draws a four-row statusline under the prompt of a terminal AI coding
  session: a context window meter with tokens and cost, 5-hour and 7-day rate-limit
  gauges, a gate verdict, a wall of teammates and the agents running in parallel. It is
  bash and Python 3 (standard library only), makes no network request, calls no model,
  and installs without replacing a status line you already have. It is part of hmd.
authors:
  - given-names: RJ
    alias: randomittin
repository-code: "https://github.com/randomittin/hmd-statusline"
url: "https://runheimdall.dev"
keywords:
